---
import PatternLayout from "../../layouts/PatternLayout.astro";
---

<PatternLayout
  title="Dark Mode"
  assumption="ThemeProvider + Context + useState"
  technique="CSS light-dark() + color-scheme + custom command (--toggle-theme) + localStorage"
  layer="1-2"
  jsShipped="inline <script> only"
>
  <p class="mb-4">
    Use the <strong>Dark / Light</strong> button in the top-right corner. The preference
    persists across all pages via <code>localStorage</code>.
  </p>

  <h3 class="mb-4">How It Works</h3>
  <ol class="pl-6 list-decimal mb-6 space-y-1">
    <li>
      Every color token in <code>@theme</code> is a <code>light-dark()</code> pair,
      resolved by <code>color-scheme</code> on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>
    </li>
    <li>
      With nothing stored, <code>color-scheme: light dark</code> follows <code
        >prefers-color-scheme</code
      > — no script involved, so it works with JavaScript off
    </li>
    <li>
      Inline <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> reads <code
        >localStorage</code
      > before paint and pins <code>.light</code> or <code>.dark</code> — no flash
    </li>
    <li>
      The button sends a <code>--toggle-theme</code> command to <code
        >&lt;html&gt;</code
      >; its label switches through the <code>dark:</code> variant, not script
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h3 class="mb-4">Sample Content</h3>
  <div class="grid gap-4 max-w-[500px]">
    <div class="p-4 bg-surface border border-border rounded-md">
      <strong>Surface</strong> — bg-surface + border-border
    </div>
    <div class="p-4 bg-surface-alt rounded-md">
      <strong>Surface Alt</strong> — bg-surface-alt
    </div>
    <div class="p-4 bg-primary text-on-primary rounded-md">
      <strong>Primary</strong> — bg-primary + text-on-primary
    </div>
    <div class="p-4 bg-danger text-on-danger rounded-md">
      <strong>Danger</strong> — bg-danger + text-on-danger
    </div>
    <div class="p-4 bg-success text-on-success rounded-md">
      <strong>Success</strong> — bg-success + text-on-success
    </div>
    <p class="text-muted text-sm">
      All these colors switch automatically through <code>color-scheme</code>.
      No per-component logic needed.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!--
    Demo note: This uses localStorage + JS class toggle.
    Production CRZ pattern: store preference in a cookie, read server-side
    in Layout frontmatter, and render <html data-theme={theme}> during SSR.
    See Sieve skill "Dark Mode" section for the cookie-based approach.
  -->
</PatternLayout>
